\subsubsection{System Comparison: AI-Pedia vs. NotebookLM vs. Dumb Student}
The core evaluation compared AI-Pedia against both baselines on 20 standardized tasks (5 per topic area). Each task involved: (i) uploading the test corpus, (ii) issuing a query requiring resource discovery and synthesis (e.g., ``Find resources to help me understand transformer attention mechanisms''), and (iii) rating the output quality.

Table \ref{tab:system_comparison} shows the results. AI-Pedia outperformed both baselines on recommendation relevance (Precision@5: 0.72 vs. 0.58 for NotebookLM and 0.41 for Dumb Student) and resource diversity (4.2 distinct sources vs. 2.1 and 1.8). NotebookLM performed reasonably well on explanation quality but rarely discovered external resources beyond the uploaded corpus. The Dumb Student baseline confirmed that the full pipeline contributes substantially: removing TF-IDF + MMR, AI filtering, and CBF ranking reduced Precision@5 by 43\%.

Fig. \ref{fig:precision_comparison} visualizes the Precision@5 comparison across topic areas, showing that AI-Pedia consistently outperformed both baselines.

